    <statement><p>Given that <m>f(4.9) = -1</m> and <m>f(5.2) = 5.9</m>, approximate
<m>f'(4.9)</m>.</p>
<p><m>f'(4.9) \approx</m> <fillin characters="15" name="AnSwEr0001"/>.</p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>23</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p>For small values of <m>h</m>, 
 <m>f'(c) \approx \frac{f(c+h) - f(c)}{h}</m>.
In this problem, <m>c = 4.9</m>, and <m>h = 5.2 - 4.9 = 0.3</m>.
<m>\displaystyle{  f'(4.9) \approx \frac{f(5.2) - f(4.9)}{0.3}
  = \frac{5.9  + 1}{0.3}
  = 23.
}</m></p>
</solution>
